From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: 32-bit code that loads FS again keeps its TEB; no 16-bit
 kernel without an LDT (Wine patches 0928, 0929)

A 32-bit game on the native WoW64 CPU that loaded FS again got the
low half of the host thread pointer as its base instead of its TEB, and
its next %fs: access faulted (Fallout 1 and 2 in GetStdHandle, at
FF81C098). Such a fault now gets the TEB's base back and the
instruction runs again.

A game that looked up kernel32's UTRegister loaded Wine's 16-bit kernel,
whose first LDT entry ended the game, since the console has no LDT
(Brian Lara International Cricket 2007). NtSetLdtEntries now fails on
the console, krnl386.exe16 doesn't load, and the lookup fails as on a
system without 16-bit support.
---
